{"n": 745, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "745.webp", "text": "37-15\nRIDE LEVEL CONTROL / CIRCULATING SYSTEM\n\nDescription\n\nRide control has the task of keeping the rear end of the car at a certain\nlevel regardless of the payload (up to maximum axle load). A piston-type\npump bolted on the power steering pump provides the system with\nnecessary pressure. The flow of oil produced permanently by the pump is\ndistributed to the line leading to the pressure reservoirs and a return line\nby a mechanically operated regulating valve depending on payload and\nride level. Ride level information for the regulating valve is taken from the\nrear axle stabilizer. Loading the car causes the suspension to bottom and\nin turn the stabilizer to turn. A control valve in the regulating valve is\nturned to lift position with help of a lever with regulating rod. The turning\nof the stabilizer is reduced as the rear end of the car lifts, which in turn\nmeans that the control valve in the regulating valve is also turned back to\nnormal position continuously. After reaching the nominal ride tevel the\ncontrol valve will be back in normal position and the oil flows direct into\nreturn (circulation).\n\nAfter reaching the maximum permissible rear axle load, a pressure safety\nvalve in the regulating valve prevents a further increase of pressure in\nspring struts and pressure reservoirs, so that the rear end of an\noverloaded car will drop.\n\nThe stabilizer is turned in opposite direction when unloading the car. The\ncontrol valve in the regulating valve is turned to lower position, so that the\noil under pressure in spring struts and pressure reservoirs can flow into\nreturn. The control valve will be back in normal position after reaching the\nnominal ride level.\n\nA. low pressure valve in the regulating valve prevents dropping the\npressure in spring struts and pressure reservoirs below the minimum\npressure while lifting the car.\n\nThe oil forced out by piston rods of single-pipe shock absorbers is pushed\nback and forth between the spring struts and pressure reservoirs while\ndriving each time the suspension of rear wheels bottoms and rebounds.\nThe gas cushion of the pressure reservoirs is then compressed and\nreleased alternately, producing the effect of gas pressure struts, which is\napplied parallel to the coil springs of the spring struts.", "words": [["37-15", 0.4529, 0.0345, 0.5157, 0.0577], ["RIDE", 0.2619, 0.0676, 0.2969, 0.1041], ["LEVEL", 0.3034, 0.0676, 0.3455, 0.1041], ["CONTROL", 0.3546, 0.0676, 0.4179, 0.1041], ["/", 0.424, 0.0736, 0.4316, 0.0928], ["CIRCULATING", 0.4382, 0.0736, 0.5314, 0.0928], ["SYSTEM", 0.5405, 0.0676, 0.5988, 0.1041], ["Description", 0.2644, 0.1578, 0.3414, 0.1757], ["Ride", 0.2644, 0.1996, 0.2938, 0.2142], ["control", 0.3009, 0.2003, 0.3485, 0.2149], ["has", 0.3556, 0.2003, 0.3794, 0.2149], ["the", 0.3865, 0.2003, 0.4073, 0.2149], ["task", 0.4144, 0.2009, 0.4412, 0.2149], ["of", 0.4483, 0.2009, 0.4615, 0.2155], ["keeping", 0.4686, 0.2009, 0.5208, 0.2188], ["the", 0.5284, 0.2016, 0.5491, 0.2155], ["rear", 0.5562, 0.2036, 0.5831, 0.2149], ["end", 0.5892, 0.2009, 0.6145, 0.2149], ["of", 0.6211, 0.2003, 0.6342, 0.2149], ["the", 0.6413, 0.2009, 0.6621, 0.2149], ["car", 0.6692, 0.2036, 0.69, 0.2142], ["at", 0.6971, 0.2016, 0.7087, 0.2149], ["a", 0.7163, 0.2029, 0.7234, 0.2142], ["certain", 0.7305, 0.2003, 0.7776, 0.2142], ["level", 0.2644, 0.2208, 0.2948, 0.2354], ["regardless", 0.3019, 0.2215, 0.3728, 0.2394], ["of", 0.3794, 0.2215, 0.3921, 0.2361], ["the", 0.3987, 0.2215, 0.4195, 0.2361], ["payload", 0.4265, 0.2221, 0.4787, 0.2401], ["(up", 0.4858, 0.2221, 0.5071, 0.2401], ["to", 0.5137, 0.2235, 0.5263, 0.2367], ["maximum", 0.5334, 0.2215, 0.5988, 0.2367], ["axle", 0.6059, 0.2215, 0.6327, 0.2361], ["load).", 0.6398, 0.2215, 0.6768, 0.2387], ["A", 0.6839, 0.2215, 0.6935, 0.2354], ["piston-type", 0.7001, 0.2215, 0.7781, 0.2394], ["pump", 0.2639, 0.2454, 0.3024, 0.2599], ["bolted", 0.3131, 0.242, 0.3546, 0.2566],